# Git Control Rule

- Do not run git commands unless the user explicitly asks in this chat.
- Never run `git push` unless the user explicitly asks for push right now.
- Never auto-commit after code changes.
- After edits, stop and ask the user whether they want to handle git in Cursor UI.
- If user asks for git status/diff information, report findings without pushing.
- Do not run destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, force push, checkout discard) unless explicitly requested.
